<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | DollarAngle"
  description="Learn how DollarAngle handles newsletter signups, analytics data and information submitted through the site."
>
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p>DollarAngle aims to collect only the information needed to operate the site, understand its audience and deliver the weekly newsletter subscribers request.</p><p><strong>Last updated:</strong> October 8, 2026</p></div></section>

<section class="section" style="padding-top:10px"><div class="container prose-wrap"><article class="prose">
<h2>Information you provide</h2>
<p>If you subscribe to the DollarAngle newsletter, we collect the email address you provide and your subscription status. If other forms are enabled in the future, we may also collect information you choose to submit, such as your name, email address and message.</p>

<h2>Weekly newsletter</h2>
<p>DollarAngle's newsletter is intended to be sent once per week. We use your email address to deliver that newsletter and manage your subscription. You can unsubscribe at any time using the unsubscribe option included in newsletter emails.</p>
<p>Newsletter subscriber information is processed using Resend, our email delivery and contact-management provider.</p>

<h2>Analytics and device information</h2>
<p>DollarAngle uses Vercel Web Analytics to understand how the site is used. Analytics may include information such as pages viewed, referring websites, browser and device type, country or approximate location, and campaign parameters such as UTM tags.</p>
<p>We use this information to understand which content readers find useful, improve the site and evaluate how visitors discover DollarAngle. We do not use analytics data to provide personalized financial advice.</p>

<h2>Hosting and service providers</h2>
<p>DollarAngle is hosted on Vercel. Service providers may process limited information on our behalf when providing hosting, analytics, security, email delivery or related infrastructure services. These providers process data under their own terms and privacy practices.</p>

<h2>How we use information</h2>
<p>We use collected information to operate and secure the website, deliver the weekly newsletter to subscribers, understand site performance, measure content and distribution effectiveness, respond to legitimate requests when contact tools are available, and comply with applicable legal obligations.</p>

<h2>How we share information</h2>
<p>DollarAngle does not sell subscriber email addresses. We may share information with service providers that help operate the website and newsletter, or when disclosure is required by law, necessary to protect the site or users, or connected with a legitimate business transfer.</p>

<h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
<p>DollarAngle currently uses analytics and hosting technologies needed to operate and measure the site. If advertising, affiliate tracking or additional cookie-based tools are introduced later, this policy and any required consent controls will be updated before those tools are used where required.</p>

<h2>Data retention</h2>
<p>We retain newsletter subscriber information while a subscription remains active and for a reasonable period afterward when needed for suppression, compliance, security or record-keeping purposes. Analytics and infrastructure providers may retain technical data according to their own retention settings and policies.</p>

<h2>Your choices and privacy rights</h2>
<p>You may unsubscribe from the newsletter at any time. Depending on where you live, applicable privacy law may also give you rights to request access to, correction of, or deletion of certain personal information, or to object to or restrict certain processing.</p>
<p>Privacy requests can be initiated through the <a href="/contact">DollarAngle Contact page</a>. We may need to verify a request before acting on it.</p>

<h2>International processing</h2>
<p>DollarAngle serves readers in multiple countries and uses service providers that may process information in countries other than your own. Where applicable, those providers are responsible for the safeguards required for their processing activities.</p>

<h2>Children's privacy</h2>
<p>DollarAngle is a general financial education publication and is not directed to children. We do not knowingly seek to collect personal information from children through the newsletter.</p>

<h2>Financial information</h2>
<p>DollarAngle does not ask newsletter subscribers to provide bank account numbers, brokerage credentials, passwords or other financial account login information. Do not submit sensitive financial credentials through DollarAngle forms.</p>

<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>We may update this Privacy Policy when our services, providers or legal obligations change. The latest version will be posted on this page with an updated date.</p>

<blockquote><strong>Note:</strong> This policy describes DollarAngle's current website and newsletter practices. It is informational and is not a substitute for legal advice.</blockquote>
